    "body": "## Problem\r\nNeovim (and Vim) do not support indenting by tabs and aligning with spaces out of the box.\r\n\r\n```\r\n:set eta sw=4 ts=4 list lcs=tab:> ,space:.\r\n\r\nint.main().{\r\n>   struct.MyStruct.{\r\n>   >   int.....num;....//.my.number\r\n>   >   char....c;......//.my.character\r\n>   };\r\n}\r\n```\r\nwhen `'tabstop'` length changes alignment will not break\r\n```\r\n:set ts=8\r\n\r\nint.main().{\r\n>       struct.MyStruct.{\r\n>       >       int.....num;....//.my.number\r\n>       >       char....c;......//.my.character\r\n>       };\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\n## Solution\r\nAdd `'expandtabalign'` (`'eta'`) option that expands tabs to spaces like `'expandtab'`, but only in non-indentation region of line. Make `:retab` and visual block shifts honour `'eta'` setting.\r\n\r\nFeature is implemented as an option because it is more elegant and integrates with features like `:retab` or visual block mode easier than plugin. Plugin would also need to re-implement `<Tab>` insertion affected by options like `smarttab`,`softtabstop`, etc. Change in C code itself is pretty compact (around 20 lines, rest is option scaffolding) and only extends a few already existing conditions for `expandtab`. \r\n\r\nI commit to maintaining and supporting this feature long-term if merged. ",
