        {
            "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
            "body": "@justinmk \r\n\r\n> does 'vartabstop' address this?\r\n\r\nNo, `varstop` does not allow to switch from tabs to spaces after first non whitespace character.\r\n\r\nIf question is if 'vartabstop' is honoured - yes. Implementation of this does not change any indentation behavior set by other options, it does exactly same as 'expandtab', but only in non-indentation (alignment) portion of line. \r\n\r\n`:set noet eta ts=4 sw=4 vts=4,8,16 listchars=tab:>-,trail:. list` will look like:\r\n``` text\r\n>--->------->---------------X...............\r\n>---Y       Z...............\r\n```",
